  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I had this idea a week ago.\nWhy not add an option in the SDK, that allows a user to upload multiple animation overrides, to a single character. \nThis would only be for things like facial expressions, unless there is a coding god at VrChat, that can make a way for new objects to be added to the avatar, position itself like you have it in Unity's hierarchy, and check to make sure that the added object doesn't push the character over 20,000 Poly's.\nI picture a new button/tab being added to the avatar section of the menu, that reads \"Current Avatar\" and this new menu has a few things inside:\n1.) A drop down box that allows you to select the uploaded animation overrides, and set them as Standing, or Sitting overrides.\n2.) An option to reset your descriptor view position. I picture this to be like setting up your full body tracking, where your character goes into a T-pose, and you move yourself where you would like your view point to be.\n3.) A avatar scale slider, having a restriction of, to big and to small. I'd be nice to have for when you drop an object and your not small enough to pick it back up, or when you go to something like a rollercoaster world, and your avatar is to big/short to see over the seat.\n4.) A mirror that can be toggled on and off, and is activated by pulling up your hand menu.\n5.) And lastly, a few fun options, like something that makes your avatar 2D.\n\nThis would be something nice to have once all of the important matters are taken care of.\nI feel as if this would clean up your avatar menu, make uploading quicker (by not having to upload the same avatar again, and adding something like \"Gesture2\" on the name, or uploading the same avatar, just to have a different size), and adding a few new options to increase the satisfaction that users get from there uploads.",
